@startuml
' STM-01 Working copy and immutable revisions; scope: editor save and restore; FR-DOC-002, FR-DOC-003. SOURCE NOT RENDER-VALIDATED.
title STM-01 Working copy and immutable revisions
[*] --> CleanWorkingCopy : open an immutable revision
CleanWorkingCopy --> DirtyWorkingCopy : author edits locally
DirtyWorkingCopy --> Saving : submit expected revision and operation key
Saving --> CleanWorkingCopy : durable commit creates new immutable revision; no further edits
Saving --> DirtyWorkingCopy : commit succeeds but newer local edits remain
Saving --> Unsaved : failure or stale version
Unsaved --> Saving : explicit retry after review
CleanWorkingCopy --> Restoring : select prior immutable revision with expected current version
Restoring --> CleanWorkingCopy : commit creates a new immutable revision
Restoring --> Unsaved : conflict or failed restore; history unchanged
note right of CleanWorkingCopy
Every acknowledged revision is immutable.
Further edits modify a separate working copy;
restore creates another revision, not an overwrite.
end note
note right of Unsaved
Local recovery is offered only when verified;
otherwise warn and offer copy/export where possible.
end note
legend right
Arrow = permitted transition with guard or action.
Unlisted transitions are rejected and audited where appropriate.
endlegend
@enduml

