@startuml
' STM-05 Conversion job; scope: job lifecycle and attempt fencing; FR-FMT-001. SOURCE NOT RENDER-VALIDATED.
title STM-05 Conversion job
[*] --> Queued
Queued --> Running : lease and fresh fencing token
Running --> Validating : attempt output staged privately
Validating --> Succeeded : checks pass; fenced artifact and report committed
Running --> Failed : terminal failure; retain prior artifact
Validating --> Failed : validation fails; retain prior artifact
Queued --> Cancelled : authorized cancellation
Running --> Cancelled : cancel and invalidate worker lease/token
Validating --> Cancelled : cancel and fence finalization
Running --> Queued : transient retry schedules new attempt and fencing token
Validating --> Queued : transient retry schedules new attempt and fencing token
Failed --> [*] : terminal job; retry/correction creates new authorized job
Cancelled --> [*] : terminal job; restart requires a new authorized job
Succeeded --> [*]
note right of Cancelled
A stale worker cannot publish an artifact after cancellation.
Attempts have separate identifiers and staged outputs.
Dead-letter delivery is an operational queue, not a job state.
end note
legend right
